      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining OAuth Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google as the OAuth provider. I'm focusing on crafting the `oauth_callback.py` file to manage the authorization code exchange process for Google's OAuth flow. The concrete implementation will ensure the correct provider identifier is included.\n\n\n**Implementing Token Exchange**\n\nNow I'm diving into crafting the `oauth_callback.py` script. The goal is to get the Python script up and running, so it can handle the OAuth callback flow from Google. I'm focusing on the HTTP requests for authorization code exchange using the `requests` library. Specifically, I'm integrating Google's OAuth endpoints. I'm working on including the appropriate Google-specific identifiers, with environment variables.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865423800,
          "start": 1789865420968
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc4ae8a80017DEBK7a5xxA0Ph",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc4ae42d001vjpXypYkXZ7c53",
