    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining OAuth Flow**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google as the OAuth provider and will be implementing an authorization-code login within the Python script, `start_oauth_login.py`. I'm focusing on making the provider selection explicit in the code. Now I'm preparing to specify the libraries I will use in the script.\n\n\n**Constructing Authorization URL**\n\nI've zeroed in on the initial script, `start_oauth_login.py`, and selected Google as the OAuth provider. My focus is now on constructing the authorization URL. I'm nailing down the necessary parameters: endpoints, client details, and scopes. I intend to use the `requests` library to build the URL and print it for the user to initiate the login flow. I'm focusing on defining the Google OAuth 2.0 endpoints within the code as the first step.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865418826,
          "start": 1789865415166
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
